## Why This Is Asked
Scenario tests Azure-native, region-conscious design with strict data residency, cross-tenant isolation, and cost control.

## Key Concepts
- Region-bound data planes, tenant isolation, data residency, BYOK, DR, cost levers
- Ingest, processing, and serving layers using Event Hubs, Data Lake, Synapse
- Governance via RBAC, Purview, and Key Vault

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function for tenant-scoped storage
function routeEvent(event){
  const t = event.tenantId;
  // route to tenant partition; security checks omitted for brevity
  return storeInTenantPartition(t, event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement cross-region read-heavy dashboards while preserving residency?
- What failure scenarios would you test and how would you roll back changes without data loss?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to map a beginner pipeline to real Azure services under data residency constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Event Hubs ingestion
- Azure Functions processing
- Cosmos DB with Row-Level Security
- Power BI per-tenant dashboards
- EU data residency and BYOK
- DR and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function (JS) sketch: read EventHub message and write to Cosmos with tenant partition
module.exports = async function(context, messages){
  for (const m of messages){
    const item = { id: m.id, tenantId: m.tenantId, ...m.payload };
    await cosmosContainer.items.upsert(item);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate tenant isolation and data residency? 
- How would you monitor costs and add capacity planning?
